          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari |Grade 9| Part I"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.108,
            0.887,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The circle is a beautiful and tantalising shape. After mastering these basic properties, you will get a feel for the symmetries of a circle and the properties of chords, the angles they subtend, the distances of chords from the centre, and angles subtended by arcs at the centre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.186,
            0.886,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Next year you will study many more interesting and beautiful such results about circles. Stay tuned — the best is yet to come!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.304,
            0.262,
            0.692,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "End-of-Chapter Exercises"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.305,
            0.886,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. In a circle, a chord is 5 cm away from the centre. If the radius of the circle is 13 cm, what is the length of the chord?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.348,
            0.886,
            0.406
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. An arc of a circle subtends an angle of 70° at the centre. What is the measure of the angle subtended by the arc at a point on the circle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.41,
            0.886,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The diameter of a circle is 26 cm. A chord of length 24 cm is drawn in the circle. Find the distance from the centre of the circle to the chord."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.476,
            0.886,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A circle has a radius of 15 cm. A chord is drawn. The distance from the centre of the circle to the chord is 9 cm. What is the length of the chord?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.543,
            0.885,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Prove that the perpendicular bisector of a chord passes through the centre of the circle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.59,
            0.884,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. The diameter of a circle is AB. Point C is on the circumference. What is the measure of the ∠ACB? Explain your reasoning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.637,
            0.886,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral inscribed in a circle. If ∠A measures 75°, what is the measure of ∠C? If ∠B measures 110°, what is the measure of ∠D?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.703,
            0.886,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Quadrilateral PQRS is inscribed in a circle. If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{P} = (2x + 10)^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{R} = (3x - 20)^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , find the value of x and the measures of ∠P and ∠R."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.77,
            0.886,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. The distance of a chord of length 16 cm from the centre of a circle is 6 cm. Find the radius of the circle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.817,
            0.852,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. A cyclic quadrilateral has sides 5, 5, 12, 12 units. Find its area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.845,
            0.886,
            0.885
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "*11. Consider a cyclic quadrilateral. Without drawing its circumcircle, how can we find out whether the centre of the circumcircle lies"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
